# The build context for `backend/Dockerfile`, which is the repository root.
#
# This repository's builders -- verified against podman 5.4.2 / buildah
# 1.39.3 only, and T12 will exercise a different one, which is the builder
# this claim needs to hold for -- read this file because it is named after
# the Dockerfile and sits beside it; a plain `backend/.dockerignore` would be
# read only if the context were `backend/`, which it cannot be -- the
# dependency tree comes from the workspace lockfile at the repository root.
# See `scripts/images.test.ts`.
#
# Bounded: these patterns reach the `build` stage of the Dockerfile only, and
# the runtime stage copies `.medusa/server` selectively rather than the build
# context wholesale -- a decoy file that reaches the build context (a stray
# `backend/secrets.json`, `env.local` or `id_rsa` not matched below) still
# cannot reach the image that ships unless something in the Dockerfile copies
# it in by name.

# Build output and dependency trees. Every one of these is produced inside the
# image from the lockfile; a copy from the developer's machine would silently
# replace it with whatever that machine happens to have.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.medusa
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Version control, CI definitions and hooks. None of it is application code.
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
.github

# Tests and configuration that exist to run them.
**/tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/vitest.config.ts
**/vitest.config.mts

# Design masters, in case one is ever committed by mistake -- this repository
# ships web derivatives only.
**/*.psd
**/*.ai
**/*.sketch
**/*.fig
**/*.xcf
**/*.afdesign
**/*.afphoto
**/*.tif
**/*.tiff

# Prose, plans and local environment files. Named patterns only -- `.env` and
# `.env.*`, not every shape a secret can take. `backend/secrets.json`,
# `env.local` and `id_rsa` are none of these and do reach the build context;
# see the bounding note above for why that does not reach the image.
**/*.md
docs
**/.env
**/.env.*

# The other workspace. Its `package.json` is re-included because npm reads
# every workspace manifest before it resolves anything, even when installing
# only this one.
storefront
!storefront/package.json
